      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "χMT of 1Tb decreases with cooling due to Stark-level depopulation, reaching 12.57 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K. Magnetization at 2 K/5 T is 13.19 Nβ, below the free-ion expectation because of anisotropy. AC susceptibility in 0.2 T dc field shows well-resolved χM′ and χM″ maxima and two relaxation processes (thermal and QTM); no frequency-range maxima in χM″ vs frequency and no Cole–Cole maxima above ca. 3 K. Field-induced slow relaxation/SMM-like behavior is described as distinct but poor at very low temperature.",
