        "summary": "Room-temperature χMT=43.67 cm3 K mol−1 agrees with three Dy(III) ions. χMT is nearly constant to 25 K then falls to 23.0 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K (1 T), while 0.1 T data show an upturn suggestive of weak ferromagnetic coupling or Zeeman effects. M=17.0 Nβ at 2 K/5 T. AC data in 0.2 T show frequency-dependent χM′ and χM″ maxima around 2–3.5 K; Cole–Cole fits over 1.8–2.87 K give Ueff=5.4 K and τ=9.6×10−6 s, indicating poor field-induced SMM behavior.",
